// The inline markup wrappers and the headings around them.

--- strong ---
a *bold* word
│ <p>a <strong>bold</strong> word</p>

--- emph ---
a _slanted_ word
│ <p>a <em>slanted</em> word</p>

--- underline ---
#underline[underlined]
│ <p><u>underlined</u></p>

--- nested-markup ---
*bold with _emphasis_ inside*
│ <p><strong>bold with <em>emphasis</em> inside</strong></p>

--- headings ---
= One

== Two

=== Three
│ <h1 id="one">One</h1>
│ <h2 id="two">Two</h2>
│ <h3 id="three">Three</h3>

--- heading-with-markup ---
= A *bold* title
│ <h1 id="a-bold-title">A <strong>bold</strong> title</h1>

--- heading-depth-past-six ---
// HTML stops at h6, so a document nested deeper keeps its structure and loses
// only the distinction the last level would have made.
======= Seven
│ <h6 id="seven">Seven</h6>

--- markup-in-heading ---
== Mixing #underline[styles] and _emphasis_
│ <h2 id="mixing-styles-and-emphasis">Mixing <u>styles</u> and <em>emphasis</em></h2>
